  "question": {
    "text": "Ques:\n$\\sigma$ is the uniform surface charge density of a thin spherical shell of radius $R$. The electric field at any point on the surface of the spherical shell is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\sigma / \\epsilon_o R$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\sigma / \\epsilon_o$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\sigma / 4 \\epsilon_o$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\sigma / 2 \\epsilon_o$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0060_0f2b730d2daf.png\"><br />By Gauss law $\\int \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{E}} \\cdot \\mathrm{d} \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{A}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{q}_{\\mathrm{in}}}{\\varepsilon_0}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{EdA}=\\frac{\\sigma \\times \\mathrm{dA}}{\\varepsilon_0} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{E}=\\frac{\\sigma}{\\varepsilon_0}\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}